<!--
  Customer360 — Salesforce-hosted MCP server (relationship-level twin of the
  deal-level CreditMemoExperinece server; kept as a separate server per the
  architecture review — relationship vs deal is a clean boundary, not merged).

  Schema confirmed against Salesforce's own Apr/May 2026 docs+blog (GA Apr 29
  2026), a real working example already in this org (CreditMemoExperinece),
  AND the live Tooling API describe of McpServerToolDefinition /
  McpServerToolApiDefinition (sf sobject describe —use-tooling-api,
  2026-07-01) after a dry-run NPE on a missing required field surfaced it.
  No isActive, no implementationClass — those do not exist on this metadata
  type. Each tool is a plain Apex class with one global @InvocableMethod;
  Salesforce auto-publishes it to the API Catalog and this file references it
  by apiIdentifier "aa:apex-{ClassName}".

  To add a tool:
    1. Verify every object/field against the live org first (getObjectSchema)
       — do not assume field names carry over from another nCino org.
    2. Write a new Apex class with exactly one @InvocableMethod
       (label + description set on the annotation).
    3. Add a new tools block below (toolName + apiDefinition/apiIdentifier/
       apiSource/operation) — "tools" is a REPEATED top-level element, one
       per tool. A McpServerToolDefinition only accepts ONE apiDefinition
       child (nesting multiple in one tools block fails deploy with "Element
       apiDefinition is duplicated"), and toolName is REQUIRED (its absence
       fails deploy with a server-side NPE, not a clear schema message).
    4. Deploy both files.
-->
<McpServerDefinition xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <description>Commercial Credit Customer 360 — relationship-level read surface (nCino+FSC, run-as-user). Ownership/beneficial-ownership graph, exposure rollups, covenants, collateral coverage, whitespace, structural EWS signals for the customer/obligor group.</description>
    <masterLabel>Customer 360</masterLabel>
    <tools>
        <toolName>Customer360Snapshot</toolName>
        <apiDefinition>
            <apiIdentifier>aa:apex-Customer360Snapshot</apiIdentifier>
            <apiSource>API_CATALOG</apiSource>
            <operation>Customer360Snapshot</operation>
        </apiDefinition>
    </tools>
    <tools>
        <toolName>Customer360RelationshipGraph</toolName>
